<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Goliath</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Goliath is the Philistine giant of Gath in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>, killed by the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sling">sling</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-elah">Valley of Elah</a> in the story told in 1 Samuel 17. The episode became a proverbial image of a weak opponent defeating a strong one. An inscription of the 10th or 9th century BCE found at Tell es-Safi, the site of Gath, contains two names etymologically similar to Goliath.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/goliath.jpg" alt="Goliath" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osmar Schindler (1869-1927) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Osmar_Schindler_David_und_Goliath.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
